exports[`CLI help interface for 'oauth cimd delete' should be expected english 1`] = `
"Usage: frodo oauth cimd delete [options] [host] [realm] [username] [password]

Delete CIMD profiles.

Arguments:
  host                       AM base URL, e.g.: https://cdk.iam.example.com/am.
                             To use a connection profile, just specify a unique
                             substring or alias.
  realm                      Realm. Specify realm as '/' for the root realm or
                             'realm' or '/parent/child' otherwise. (default:
                             "alpha" for Identity Cloud tenants, "/" otherwise.)
  username                   Username to login with. Must be an admin user with
                             appropriate rights to manage authentication
                             journeys/trees. If given without a password, and it
                             matches the username already stored in the
                             connection profile for the target host, frodo uses
                             that profile's stored password instead of requiring
                             it on the command line.
  password                   Password.

Options:
  -a, --all                  Delete all CIMD profiles. Cannot be used with -i.
  --allow-failures           Report operations that fail, but still exit with
                             code 0. Without this option the command runs every
                             operation, prints a summary of what failed and
                             exits with code 1.
  --dry-run                  Show which CIMD profiles would be deleted and
                             delete nothing. Only with -a. Cannot be used with
                             -i.
  -i, --agent-id <agent-id>  Agent id: the id of the CIMD profile. Cannot be
                             used with -a or --dry-run. (pick from CIMD profile)
  -y, --yes                  Do not ask for confirmation before deleting all
                             CIMD profiles. Required with -a when there is no
                             terminal.
  -h, --help                 Help
  -hh, --help-more           Help with all options.
  -hhh, --help-all           Help with all options, environment variables, and
                             usage examples.

Rule:
  one of -a, --all | -i, --agent-id <agent-id> is required -- choose what to delete

"
`;
